# Lexicons

Use a lexicon to check a word, a punctuation mark, a number or a Home Assistant term. They settle questions the [writing guidelines](../writing-guidelines/index.html) do not.

| Lexicon | Use it for |
| --- | --- |
| [A to Z General](a-to-z.html) | Capital letters, punctuation, numbers, dates, times, units and the words used in civica content |
| [A to Z Technical](technical-a-to-z.html) | Home Assistant terms: entities, states, attributes, automations, cards, settings and their labels |

## How to use them

1. Look up the word in A to Z Technical first. If it is not there, look in A to Z General.
2. If a word is in neither, use the rule in [Use clear language](../writing-guidelines/clear-language.html).
3. If a rule needs to change, record it as an [exception](../publish-update-retire/update.html) and say why.

Both lexicons keep native Home Assistant labels as they are. A rule about wording never changes a translation, a screen label or a name someone gave a device.
